Offer the system folder picker from File > Open Folder on Android.

Open Folder in the web workbench is the quick input that asks for a path. On a phone that
dialog starts in the app's own storage and lists what the app itself can read. A folder in
shared storage (Documents, Download, an SD card) is empty there, because Android hides what
other apps saved from a path and only the system picker grants access to it. The picker is
the saf-bridge command vscodroid.openFolderFromDevice, but only the command palette, the
remote indicator menu and the empty Explorer reached it. The File menu, Ctrl+K Ctrl+O, the
palette's own Open Folder and the Explorer's Open Folder button all end in pickFolderAndOpen,
and each of them showed the typed dialog.

pickFolderAndOpen now asks which one is meant when the page runs on Android and the command
is registered. "On the device" runs the picker, "In the app's storage" continues to the typed
dialog exactly as before, and dismissing the question does nothing. Open in a new window keeps
the typed dialog, because the picker opens its folder in the current window. Add Folder to
Workspace, Save As and Open File do not go through this function and are untouched.

The command is registered once the bundled extension has activated, which is a few seconds
after a page loads. Until then, and when the extension is missing, the typed dialog shows
alone, as it did before. That check is load-bearing: executeCommand on an id that nothing
registered waits up to 30 seconds for an activation event before it rejects. A question that
cannot be shown, or a command that fails, falls back to the typed dialog and logs a warning.

The typed dialog starts in the parent of the folder that is open. For a folder opened from
shared storage that is the app's copy of it under saf-mirrors, which holds nothing to open
but the copies of other folders, so "In the app's storage" started there and the way to the
projects folder was to type its path. When the folder that is open, or the last active file
when none is, is inside saf-mirrors and ~/projects exists, the dialog now starts in
~/projects (a link to the projects folder). Every other start is as before: a folder in the
projects folder starts in its parent, and with nothing open the dialog starts in the home
folder, where projects is listed.

